### Forward Proxy vs Reverse Proxy

##### What is a Proxy?
- A proxy is an intermediary server between a client and another server. 
- Proxies help with security, caching, traffic control, and anonymity. 
- Two main types: forward proxies & reverse proxy

    ![alt text](./assets/image-10.png)

##### What is a forward proxy? 
- Sits between a client and the internet (used by the clients)
- Clients connect to the forward proxy instead of directly accessing the website. 
- Can filter content provide anonymity and cache requests? 
- Common Use Cases 
    - Privacy and Anonymity: Hide User IP 
    - Content filtering (Restricts certain websites) 
    - Bypass geo restrictions: (Access region blocked content)
    - Caching: (reduce redundant requests, speed up browsing) 
    
    ![alt text](./assets/image-11.png)

##### What is a reverse proxy? 
- Sets between users and backend server (used by servers)
- Clients don't directly communicate with the backend server. Requests go through the request reverse proxy. 
- Used for load balancing, caching, security, and SSL termination 
- Common Use Cases 
    - Load balancing: distribute traffic to multiple servers 
    - Security and DDoS protection: Hide backend server blocked attacks 
    - SSL Termination:  Offload SSL Processing to Proxy 
    - Caching and compression: Reduce load on Tekken server. 

    ![alt text](./assets/image-12.png)

